  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_shutdown_executor_values",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_execute_API.c",
    "description": "During request shutdown, zend_shutdown_executor_values() calls zend_hash_graceful_reverse_destroy(&EG(symbol_table)), which invokes zend_unclean_zval_ptr_dtor()/i_zval_ptr_dtor() on symbol-table zvals. For this PoV, a corrupted/invalid zval remains in EG(symbol_table), so i_zval_ptr_dtor() reaches zend_gc_delref() with a wild zend_refcounted_h* and crashes on refcount read (zend_types.h:1351). The crash site is zend_gc_delref, but the root cause is unsafe destruction of corrupted symbol-table entries in shutdown path.",
    "conditions": "The fuzzed PHP script must drive the engine into a state where EG(symbol_table) contains an invalid refcounted zval by request end. On php-fuzz-tracing-jit, request shutdown (fuzzer_request_shutdown -> php_request_shutdown -> zend_deactivate -> shutdown_executor -> zend_shutdown_executor_values) performs graceful reverse destruction of the symbol table, and the invalid entry is destructed, triggering invalid pointer dereference in zend_gc_delref."
  },
